 are not  physically distancing  and we are the country right now is on a  precipice  with children back at school students  going back to universities people being  encouraged to go  to work and with winter coming we are in  real danger if we don't get the  messaging right  that we will have a resurgence but do  you accept that the government is also  dancing on the head of a pin and it has  to deal with the mental health of the  country as well and  a lot of people have struggled with  lockdown  i fully agree with that and that's why  lockdown is not the answer what we have  to do  is we have to renegotiate our  relationship with the virus and what i  mean by that  is that we have to accept and understand  that this virus is with us  it's going to be with us for a long time  to come a vaccine is not going to be a  magic bullet that suddenly takes  all the risks and dangers away and  therefore  we are going to have to change our  behaviors in order to live with the  virus around us but at the moment those  messages  about the scale of the of the  transformation in our society that's  taken place i don't think of being  communicated  anywhere near forcibly enough and that's  why people are relaxing why they are  mixing  and why they aren't practicing these  basic messages and why we are seeing  3 000 cases as we saw over the weekend  it's coming back if we're not  careful we are seeing 3 000 cases but  we're not seeing the same number of  deaths correlating  to those numbers and that's what  particularly young people is saying okay  i might get it  but it's not going to kill me  no that's absolutely right but young  people don't live in their own bubble  young people are mixing with older  people and if you  look at the hospital mortality for  example  the mortality is very tightly linked to  aa  and if a young person passes  is mixing with somebody who is for  example  over 50 or 60 or 70 years old as we will  be in our families  then that's where the danger comes 